# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it) for tonight's four-card window.
# U0: hand the four cards from production to the window. DELETE the placement through the admin API FIRST and see
# placements: [] (a warm placement is redispatched by the reconciler); only then push this job.
# platform: captures the serving container's state, env and /v1/models (read-only) into the results.
# unserve:  stops (graceful, 60 s) and removes every thatch-inference-* container (an exited one blocks every CI card step).
# reset:    all four boards together, plus the heal. It refuses while any card is held or any thatch-inference-* container
#           exists, so it cannot pull cards out from under a live or starting container.
# Nothing else changes: the drop-in stays P150x4 and thatch-serving-tt:latest stays the S2 layer; the QSFP gate goes stale
# after this reset, so no container can start on the cards even if a placement reappeared.
# Duration: status 1-2 min, platform 1 min, unserve 1-2 min, reset 3-12 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status platform unserve reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
